Qualifications

Required Qualifications

Current TS/SCI clearance with polygraph;
Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience Masters degree and 0 years of experience, 4 years of additional relevant experience may be considered in lieu of degree;
Must demonstrate flexibility and be willing and able to work on a team that supports 16x7 coverage, including weekends and holidays;
Knowledge of analytic methodologies and tradecraft, and ability to apply those skills within the intelligence cycle;
Excellent attention to detail, and willingness and ability to work within existing standard operating procedures;
Strong interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills;
Ability to effectively communicate with diverse technical and non-technical audiences;
Ability to apply critical thinking skills to resolve issues with support from leadership

Desired Qualifications

Experience supporting national-level customers;
Experience working in the customer's operational environment;
Experience leveraging customer tools and databases to develop analytic products;
Experience with social network analysis and/or dynamic network analysis

Details

Target Salary Range: $80,000 - $128,000. This represents the typical salary range for this position. Salary is determined by various factors, including but not limited to, the scope and responsibilities of the position, the individual's experience, education, knowledge, skills, and competencies, as well as geographic location and business and contract considerations. Depending on the position, employees may be eligible for overtime, shift differential, and a discretionary bonus in addition to base pay.

